<p>South Korean President Lee Jae Myung said Monday that he regretted drones sent into North Korea earlier this year, after an investigation found that South Korean government officials were involved. Seoul had initially denied any official role in the January drone incident and suggested civilians might have been responsible, but Lee said the probe later showed state involvement. Lee said the drone flights were not ordered by his government and expressed regret to Pyongyang for the tensions that followed, a notable public acknowledgment in a relationship often defined by mistrust and escalation. His statement suggests an effort to lower tensions after a sensitive cross-border episode on the Korean Peninsula.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/BFV809Yd0dWMKeRxtx9tNVXmzewVHhpYtJl_AauwGfz4Lh0m-Wv0-7pkj7Z7375xKYdfd7wDSvmIohue42wM2yKcZ4jJdU6RYdvbAOtAv4Kw5p91v-cyFhrZTq7EFHgTXYtlB4LyaKDGX6MDgagFNK1D1Zebbdv2Q-R-kJdu2c_WW4jy7ZppsoCnuvm9w1_AAbj7FilqW1Se4z2VWo63hTWpnJ_tik5zsCgpUJ4V9JF0fM2WHIWbtm48Lkgz3Lb9PzlKmSdCFw' alt='South Korean President Lee Jae Myung speaks during his new year press conference at the presidential Blue House in Seoul, South Korea, January 21, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Lee called the drone flights &#x27;irresponsible&#x27; and &#x27;reckless,&#x27; a sharper condemnation than a routine expression of regret</li><li>Reports identified the aircraft in question as a surveillance drone</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-president-says-regrets-drones-sent-to-north/a-76676137'>South Korea president says regrets drones sent to North</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3349113/south-koreas-lee-regrets-drones-sent-north-irresponsible-and-reckless'>South Korea’s Lee regrets drones sent to North: ‘irresponsible and reckless’</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/06/south-korea-s-president-regrets-reckless-drones-